course: dictionary
lesson: 4547
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Hearty can describe a laugh, a meal, a person or thanks. Context tells you which meaning to use, so read the words around it before you choose.
explain: Toad has escaped, and then he has «a hearty laugh — for the first time since he was thrown into prison». The clue is that he is free and happy again. A loud, cheerful laugh fits that feeling, so hearty means loud and cheerful here.
explain: The same word can mean something different in a different sentence. A hearty breakfast is large, warm and filling, not loud at all. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Hearty means loud, cheerful and friendly, as in a hearty laugh or a hearty welcome.
fact: Hearty can also describe food that is large, warm and filling, like a hearty breakfast or hearty soup.
fact: Hale and hearty means strong and healthy.
fact: Hearty thanks means sincere thanks, which are strongly felt.
exercise: «He gave a hearty laugh when the joke ended.» What does hearty mean here? | Cold and silent | *Loud and cheerful | Small and quiet | Sad and tired
exercise: «The farmer served a hearty breakfast of eggs, bacon and porridge.» What does hearty mean here? | Very quiet | Sad and sour | Tiny and cold | *Large, warm and filling
exercise: Grandad is still hale and hearty at ninety. What does hale and hearty mean? | Cold and wet | Ill and tired | Late for dinner | *Strong and healthy
test: «Father Christmas gave a hearty ho-ho-ho as he came down the chimney.» Which meaning fits best? | Quiet and shy | Sick and weak | Empty and cold | *Loud and cheerful
test: Ella says «hearty thanks» means thanks with no feeling at all. Why is she wrong? | *Hearty thanks means sincere thanks that are strongly felt | Hearty thanks means thanks said very quietly | Hearty means empty | Hearty thanks means thanks written on a card
exam: In «a hearty laugh — for the first time since he was thrown into prison», what clue tells you hearty means cheerful? | He is hungry | He is angry with the chasers | *He is free and happy after being in prison | He is ill and tired
